# GET /drain — step 2: drain the namespace inside ONE op.
#
# kv/list is windowed: at most `limit` keys per call, sorted after the
# `after` cursor, with `next` = the cursor for the following call ("" when
# the namespace is exhausted). Without LOOP you would need a @goto loop —
# a full stage hop per page, with every sibling op at the target scope
# re-evaluated each time. With it, this op re-runs itself:
#
#   - `after = ._page.next` is a WITH value, re-resolved before every
#     pass against the view (envelope + everything merged so far), so
#     the cursor advances by itself;
#   - passes merge with the scope-merge rules — `keys` (an array)
#     appends, `next` and `count` (scalars) take the last pass's value;
#   - the loop stops when `._page.next == ""` holds (done), at MAX
#     passes (max), on a pass error, on fuel, on the op's timeout, or
#     when a sibling halts — and the scope sees ONE merged payload
#     either way.
#
# Five seeded keys at limit 2 → three passes: [a,b] [c,d] [e]. EVERY
# "2ms" opts out of the 50ms default pause, which is sized for polls.
# What happened is written to @runtime.loop.drain = {passes, stop,
# elapsed_ms}; the responder at 300 copies it into the body.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.path == "/drain"
  EXEC "txco://kv/list"
    WITH namespace = "drain-demo",
         limit = 2,
         after = ._page.next,
         into = "_page"
  LOOP EVERY "2ms" UNTIL ._page.next == "" MAX 10
